    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d733">

                <pb facs="1013" n="889" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg889"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/49: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Child</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-30T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 30—5
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>208. <hi rendition="#italic">Aide-mémoire</hi> contained in your 159, October
                        28,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d733-f1"/> has been delivered. It is impossible
                    under existing political conditions to <pb facs="1014" n="890" xml:id="pg890"/>
                    make contact with responsible Italian officials in order to amplify by
                    conversations the purpose of the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>. As
                    soon as possible this will be done.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d733-f1" n="8" xml:id="d733-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 344, Oct. 27, to the Ambassador in France, <ref target="#pg884"
                        >p. 884</ref>. No record of a reply by the Italian Government to this <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> has been found in Department
                    files.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
